30:["$","blockquote","1",{"className":"m-0 flex flex-col gap-[var(--space-3)] border-l-4 border-line-strong pl-[var(--space-4)] text-ink-900","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"[ภาพ: ตราสัญลักษณ์ของมหาวิทยาลัยธรรมศาสตร์ มีข้อความ THAMMASAT UNIVERSITY]"}]]]}]]}]
31:["$","h3","2",{"className":"m-0 mt-[var(--space-4)]","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Thammasat University Student Activity Regulations"}]]]}]
32:["$","p","3",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Operation and Meeting of the Student Council of Thammasat University, Tha Prachan, B.E. 2569"}]]]}]
33:["$","p","4",{"id":"clause-1","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 1"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" These regulations shall be cited as the “Thammasat University Student Activity Regulations Re: Operation and Meeting of the Student Council of Thammasat University, Tha Prachan, B.E. 2569”."}]]]}]
34:["$","p","5",{"id":"clause-2","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 2"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" These regulations shall come into force from the date the Council passes an affirmative resolution of approval onwards."}]]]}]
35:["$","p","6",{"id":"clause-3","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 3"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" In these regulations"}]]]}]
36:["$","p","7",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"“Council” means the Student Council of Thammasat University, Tha Prachan."}]]]}]
37:["$","p","8",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"“President of the Council” means the President of the Student Council of Thammasat University, Tha Prachan."}]]]}]
38:["$","p","9",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"“Vice President of the Council” means the Vice President of the Student Council of Thammasat University, Tha Prachan."}]]]}]
39:["$","p","10",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"“Secretary-General” means the Secretary-General of the Student Council of Thammasat University, Tha Prachan."}]]]}]
3a:["$","p","11",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"“Deputy Secretary-General” means the Deputy Secretary-General of the Student Council of Thammasat University, Tha Prachan."}]]]}]
3b:["$","p","12",{"className":"m-0 border-t border-line pt-[var(--space-2)] text-sm text-ink-600","children":"[Page 2 of the original]"}]
3c:["$","p","13",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"“Member” means a member of the Student Council of Thammasat University, Tha Prachan."}]]]}]
3d:["$","p","14",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"“Chairman” means the chairman presiding over the meeting of the Student Council of Thammasat University, Tha Prachan."}]]]}]
3e:["$","p","15",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"“Commissioner” means an ordinary commissioner or an extraordinary commissioner of the Student Council of Thammasat University, Tha Prachan."}]]]}]
3f:["$","p","16",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"“Office of the President of the Council” means the Office of the President of the Council of the Student Council of Thammasat University, Tha Prachan."}]]]}]
40:["$","p","17",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"“Office of the Secretariat” means the Office of the Secretariat of the Student Council of Thammasat University, Tha Prachan."}]]]}]
41:["$","p","18",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"“Sub-commissioner” means a person appointed by a committee to assist in any affairs of the committee."}]]]}]
42:["$","p","19",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"“Meeting” means the meeting of the Student Council of Thammasat University, Tha Prachan."}]]]}]
43:["$","p","20",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"“The Assembly” means the assembly of the Student Council of Thammasat University, Tha Prachan."}]]]}]
44:["$","p","21",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"“Council Area” means the jurisdictional area under the responsibility of the Council, venues utilized for meetings either permanently or temporarily, the offices of the Council Executive Committee, Committees, the Office of the President of the Council, the Office of the Secretariat, and members, and shall include user accounts, chat rooms, meeting rooms, and other platforms of the Council accessed via electronic media."}]]]}]
45:["$","p","22",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"“Party” means a student party holding seats in the Council."}]]]}]
46:["$","p","23",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"“University” means Thammasat University."}]]]}]
47:["$","p","24",{"className":"m-0 border-t border-line pt-[var(--space-2)] text-sm text-ink-600","children":"[Page 3 of the original]"}]
48:["$","p","25",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"“Rules” means the Thammasat University Rules on Thammasat University Student Activities B.E. 2563."}]]]}]
49:["$","p","26",{"id":"clause-4","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 4"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" The President of the Council shall have charge and direction of the execution of these regulations and shall be empowered to issue subsequent regulations for the implementation thereof."}]]]}]
4a:["$","h4","27",{"className":"m-0 mt-[var(--space-4)]","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Chapter 1 Joint Council Coordination Committee"}]]]}]
4b:["$","p","28",{"id":"clause-5","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 5"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" There shall be a committee designated as the “Joint Council Coordination Committee,” comprising the President of the Council, or a Vice President of the Council delegated by the President, to serve as the chairman of the committee, and not more than nine other committee members appointed by the President of the Council from party members. Such appointments shall consist of at least one person per party in accordance with the respective party's resolution. In the event that the Council is constituted by only a single party, the appointment of the committee may be omitted mutatis mutandis."}]]]}]
4c:["$","p","29",{"id":"clause-6","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 6"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" A Joint Council Coordination Committee member vacates office upon"}]]]}]
4d:["$","p","30",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(1) The expiration of the Council's term or the dissolution of the Council."}]]]}]
4e:["$","p","31",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(2) Death."}]]]}]
4f:["$","p","32",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(3) Resignation."}]]]}]
50:["$","p","33",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(4) Termination of membership."}]]]}]
51:["$","p","34",{"className":"m-0 border-t border-line pt-[var(--space-2)] text-sm text-ink-600","children":"[Page 4 of the original]"}]
52:["$","p","35",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(5) The appointment of a new Joint Council Coordination Committee superseding the former."}]]]}]
53:["$","p","36",{"id":"clause-7","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 7"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" The Joint Council Coordination Committee shall possess the following powers and duties"}]]]}]
54:["$","p","37",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(1) To consider, proceed with, or coordinate matters pertaining to the meetings and affairs of the Council."}]]]}]
55:["$","p","38",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(2) To exercise other powers and duties as assigned by the President of the Council."}]]]}]
56:["$","h4","39",{"className":"m-0 mt-[var(--space-4)]","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Chapter 2 Meeting"}]]]}]
57:["$","h5","40",{"className":"m-0 mt-[var(--space-4)]","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Part 1: Meeting Procedures"}]]]}]
58:["$","p","41",{"id":"clause-8","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 8"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" The meeting shall be held openly. General students may attend to observe the meeting within the Council Area as announced by the Chairman, unless a motion for a secret meeting is requested by members constituting more than one-half of the total number of existing members of the Council, whereupon a secret meeting shall be convened."}]]]}]
59:["$","p","42",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"During a secret meeting, third parties are strictly prohibited from attending, save for those explicitly granted permission by the Chairman."}]]]}]
5a:["$","p","43",{"id":"clause-9","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 9"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" In the event of an absolute necessity to convene a meeting outside of the ordinary session, the President of the Council may summon an extraordinary session."}]]]}]
5b:["$","p","44",{"className":"m-0 border-t border-line pt-[var(--space-2)] text-sm text-ink-600","children":"[Page 5 of the original]"}]
5c:["$","p","45",{"id":"clause-10","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 10"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" The notice of meeting must be executed in writing, specifying the date, time, venue, and meeting agenda. Said notice must be communicated to the members in advance for not less than five days for an ordinary session, and not less than three days for an extraordinary session."}]]]}]
5d:["$","p","46",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Should there be an unavoidable and urgent necessity, the President of the Council shall have the discretion to issue a meeting notice at least one hour in advance."}]]]}]
5e:["$","p","47",{"id":"clause-11","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 11"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" The Secretary-General shall distribute the meeting agenda and pertinent documents alongside the meeting notice. Should the President of the Council deem it appropriate, any additional matters may be incorporated into the meeting agenda, provided that such inclusion occurs not less than one day prior to the meeting date."}]]]}]
5f:["$","p","48",{"id":"clause-12","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 12"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" The issuance of the meeting notice pursuant to Clause 10 and the distribution of documents pursuant to Clause 11 may be executed via electronic media or alternative information technology platforms, as deemed appropriate by the President of the Council, with the exception of the delivery of classified documents, which shall be governed by the procedures prescribed by the President of the Council."}]]]}]
60:["$","p","49",{"id":"clause-13","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 13"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" The meeting agenda shall be structured in the following sequence:"}]]]}]
61:["$","p","50",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(1) Interpellations."}]]]}]
62:["$","p","51",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(2) Matters informed by the Chairman."}]]]}]
63:["$","p","52",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(3) Adoption of the minutes of the meeting."}]]]}]
64:["$","p","53",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(4) Matters previously concluded by the committee."}]]]}]
65:["$","p","54",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(5) Pending matters from the previous session."}]]]}]
66:["$","p","55",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(6) Matters proposed to the assembly for consideration."}]]]}]
67:["$","p","56",{"className":"m-0 border-t border-line pt-[var(--space-2)] text-sm text-ink-600","children":"[Page 6 of the original]"}]
68:["$","p","57",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(7) Other matters."}]]]}]
69:["$","p","58",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(8) Scheduling of the subsequent Council meeting."}]]]}]
6a:["$","p","59",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"In the event that the President of the Council classifies any matter as an urgent matter, it may be placed in any sequence within the agenda; however, it shall not precede matters previously concluded by the committee, unless it entails the summoning of the President of the Student Union, the Vice President of the Student Union, an authorized representative thereof, or other individuals for the purpose of clarification or performance reporting, in which case the President of the Council may place it under (1)."}]]]}]
6b:["$","p","60",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"The filing of an interpellation against the Council Executive Committee or a Council Executive member is permissible and shall be placed under (1), provided that the interpellation is submitted to the President of the Council at least one day prior to the meeting date. The party subject to the interpellation reserves the right to elect whether or not to respond."}]]]}]
6c:["$","p","61",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"In the case of a live verbal interpellation raised before the assembly, the subject matter must relate to the interests of the University, the students, the Council, or be an issue of urgent significance. Furthermore, it must not be framed as a personal attack against any individual or group."}]]]}]
6d:["$","p","62",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"The Chairman's ruling concerning the filing of interpellations pursuant to paragraphs three and four shall be deemed absolute and final."}]]]}]
6e:["$","p","63",{"id":"clause-14","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 14"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Prior to commencing the meeting agenda, the Chairman may grant members permission to consult on matters concerning student grievances or any other issues, in accordance with the criteria and procedures prescribed by the President of the Council. The President of the Council shall subsequently forward said matters to the relevant University agency for clarification within the subsequent meeting and shall notify the members accordingly."}]]]}]
6f:["$","p","64",{"className":"m-0 border-t border-line pt-[var(--space-2)] text-sm text-ink-600","children":"[Page 7 of the original]"}]
70:["$","p","65",{"id":"clause-15","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 15"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Prior to every meeting, attending members are required to affix their signatures in designated registration documents or alternative formats, or authenticate their identity in accordance with the regulations prescribed by the President of the Council. A quorum shall be constituted when not less than one-half of the total number of existing members have registered their attendance."}]]]}]
71:["$","p","66",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Once the quorum is achieved and the signal to convene is given, the Chairman shall commence the meeting within five minutes thereafter."}]]]}]
72:["$","p","67",{"id":"clause-16","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 16"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Should a member fail to comply with Clause 15, paragraph one, without providing prior notification to the President of the Council or the Secretary-General, said member shall be deemed absent."}]]]}]
73:["$","p","68",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"If a member enters or departs the assembly while the meeting is in progress, they must immediately notify the Chairman or the Secretary-General under all circumstances."}]]]}]
74:["$","p","69",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Upon the Chairman signaling the commencement of the meeting, all persons within the assembly are strictly required to maintain order and decorum."}]]]}]
75:["$","p","70",{"id":"clause-17","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 17"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Upon the expiration of thirty minutes from the scheduled meeting time, if the number of attending members remains insufficient to constitute a quorum, the Chairman may order the postponement of the meeting."}]]]}]
76:["$","p","71",{"id":"clause-18","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 18"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" During said meeting, the assembly shall exclusively deliberate upon matters contained within the meeting agenda and must proceed in the prescribed sequence, unless the assembly resolves otherwise by an affirmative vote of not less than one-third of the quorum."}]]]}]
77:["$","p","72",{"id":"clause-19","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 19"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Any person desiring to address the assembly shall indicate their intent by raising their hand above their head. The individual may only speak upon receiving permission from the Chairman, and all remarks must be addressed solely to the Chairman."}]]]}]
78:["$","p","73",{"className":"m-0 border-t border-line pt-[var(--space-2)] text-sm text-ink-600","children":"[Page 8 of the original]"}]
79:["$","p","74",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"If it is necessary to invoke the name of another member, the speaker must expressly state \"Request permission to reference a name\" on every occasion."}]]]}]
7a:["$","p","75",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"For meetings conducted via electronic media, the Chairman shall prescribe appropriate criteria and procedures for members to manifest their intent to address the assembly."}]]]}]
7b:["$","p","76",{"id":"clause-20","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 20"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" The Chairman may consult the assembly regarding any issues, prescribe procedures for verifying the quorum, or order a recess, postponement, or adjournment of the meeting as deemed appropriate."}]]]}]
7c:["$","p","77",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Should the Chairman depart the assembly without issuing any directive and without appointing an acting substitute, the meeting shall be adjourned. Such an event must be formally recorded, and the Chairman is obligated to provide a clarification to the members concerning their departure."}]]]}]
7d:["$","p","78",{"id":"clause-21","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 21"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" The Secretary-General shall act as the drafter and reviewer of the meeting minutes."}]]]}]
7e:["$","p","79",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Following the Secretary-General's review and prior to submission for the Council's adoption, a copy of the minutes shall be made available at the Council Area or disseminated via electronic media or other information technology channels for a period of not less than three days, or by any other means deemed appropriate by the Chairman, to facilitate inspection by the members."}]]]}]
7f:["$","p","80",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"All meeting minutes must document the names of the members present, on leave, absent, the observers, and a formal record of the voting."}]]]}]
80:["$","p","81",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"A member reserves the right to request amendments to the meeting minutes to reflect factual accuracy by submitting an amendment request to the Secretary-General. Should the Secretary-General fail to implement the requested amendments, the member is entitled to"}]]]}]
81:["$","p","82",{"className":"m-0 border-t border-line pt-[var(--space-2)] text-sm text-ink-600","children":"[Page 9 of the original]"}]
82:["$","p","83",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"reaffirm the request by petitioning the Council for a ruling, which requires an affirmative resolution of not less than one-fifth of the quorum."}]]]}]
83:["$","p","84",{"id":"clause-22","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 22"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" For any meeting minutes made available or disseminated for members' inspection, if subsequent amendments are executed—whether by the committee itself or upon a member's request—the committee or the Secretary-General must formally declare such amendments to the assembly during the session wherein the Council considers the adoption of said minutes."}]]]}]
84:["$","p","85",{"id":"clause-23","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 23"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Upon the Council's adoption of any meeting minutes, the President of the Council shall affix their signature as formal evidence."}]]]}]
85:["$","p","86",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Regarding meeting minutes that have been adopted but not yet signed by the President, or minutes that remain unadopted due to the expiration of the Council's term, the Secretary-General shall document the cause thereof and shall serve as the official certifier of the accuracy of said minutes."}]]]}]
86:["$","p","87",{"id":"clause-24","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 24"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" The Council may resolve to withhold the recording of secret meeting minutes, either entirely or partially, provided that a general record of events is maintained."}]]]}]
87:["$","p","88",{"id":"clause-25","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 25"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" The disclosure of secret meeting minutes shall be subject to the assembly's deliberation and resolution. Such disclosure requires an affirmative resolution of not less than one-half of the existing members of the Council."}]]]}]
88:["$","p","89",{"id":"clause-26","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 26"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" The Secretary-General shall be responsible for publishing and disseminating the meeting minutes, excluding secret meeting minutes which the Council has resolved not to disclose."}]]]}]
89:["$","p","90",{"className":"m-0 border-t border-line pt-[var(--space-2)] text-sm text-ink-600","children":"[Page 10 of the original]"}]
8a:["$","h5","91",{"className":"m-0 mt-[var(--space-4)]","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Part 2: Submission of Motions"}]]]}]
8b:["$","p","92",{"id":"clause-27","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 27"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" A \"motion\" denotes any proposal intended for the Council to resolve or decide upon regarding the execution or continuation of any specific action."}]]]}]
8c:["$","p","93",{"id":"clause-28","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 28"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" All motions must be submitted in advance in writing to the President of the Council and must be seconded by not less than three members, except as explicitly provided otherwise within these regulations."}]]]}]
8d:["$","p","94",{"id":"clause-29","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 29"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" A motion proposing the establishment of a committee by the Council, or requesting any committee to execute activities, consider, investigate, or study any matters falling within the Council's authority and duties, if proposed by a member, must be seconded by not less than one-fourth of the total number of existing members of the Council."}]]]}]
8e:["$","p","95",{"id":"clause-30","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 30"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" A motion requesting a Council Executive member to vacate office must be seconded by not less than one-fourth of the total number of existing members of the Council."}]]]}]
8f:["$","p","96",{"id":"clause-31","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 31"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" A motion requesting a commissioner to vacate office must be proposed by the respective committee or affiliated office, accompanied by a written statement explicitly specifying the evident rationale to the President of the Council."}]]]}]
90:["$","p","97",{"id":"clause-32","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 32"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" In matters implicating significant interests of the University or the students, or in instances of urgent necessity concerning student rights and welfare, a member may propose an urgent motion for the Council's immediate consideration. An urgent motion must not resemble the nature of an interpellation and must serve the objective of compelling the Council to undertake a specific action."}]]]}]
91:["$","p","98",{"className":"m-0 border-t border-line pt-[var(--space-2)] text-sm text-ink-600","children":"[Page 11 of the original]"}]
92:["$","p","99",{"id":"clause-33","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 33"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" The President of the Council shall possess the authority to determine whether any motion constitutes an urgent motion. Upon such determination, the President shall notify the proposer of the motion, inclusive of the rationale, within three days from the date of receipt of said motion."}]]]}]
93:["$","p","100",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"The President of the Council shall place the urgent motion on the meeting agenda as an urgent matter."}]]]}]
94:["$","p","101",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"For motions determined by the President of the Council as non-urgent, the President shall proceed in accordance with Clause 34."}]]]}]
95:["$","p","102",{"id":"clause-34","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 34"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Subject to Clause 33, the President of the Council shall place the motion on the meeting agenda within seven days from the date of its receipt, in chronological order of submission. The term \"days\" herein shall be construed as days within the meeting session."}]]]}]
96:["$","p","103",{"id":"clause-35","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 35"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" The following motions are exempt from the requirement of prior written submission"}]]]}]
97:["$","p","104",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(1) A motion to consider a matter as an urgent matter."}]]]}]
98:["$","p","105",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(2) A motion to amend the meeting agenda."}]]]}]
99:["$","p","106",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(3) Motions permitted by the Chairman as deemed appropriate."}]]]}]
9a:["$","p","107",{"id":"clause-36","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 36"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" While the assembly is actively deliberating a motion, the proposal of alternative motions is strictly prohibited, with the exception of the following:"}]]]}]
9b:["$","p","108",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(1) A motion to consolidate meeting agendas of identical, similar, or related nature for concurrent consideration."}]]]}]
9c:["$","p","109",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(2) A motion to refer an issue to a committee for consideration, or to request any person to submit documents, provide factual testimony, or express opinions."}]]]}]
9d:["$","p","110",{"className":"m-0 border-t border-line pt-[var(--space-2)] text-sm text-ink-600","children":"[Page 12 of the original]"}]
9e:["$","p","111",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(3) A motion to sever or consolidate issues for consideration or resolution."}]]]}]
9f:["$","p","112",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(4) A motion to postpone consultation or consideration."}]]]}]
a0:["$","p","113",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(5) A motion to close the debate."}]]]}]
a1:["$","p","114",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(6) A motion to raise other matters for consultation or consideration."}]]]}]
a2:["$","p","115",{"id":"clause-37","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 37"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" The proposal of motions pursuant to Clause 36 (5) and (6) concurrently with one's own debate is prohibited."}]]]}]
a3:["$","p","116",{"id":"clause-38","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 38"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" In the event the assembly resolves to raise another matter for consultation or consideration, the original motion shall be deemed to have lapsed."}]]]}]
a4:["$","p","117",{"id":"clause-39","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 39"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" For motions submitted in advance in writing, the seconders shall signify their endorsement by raising their hand above their head."}]]]}]
a5:["$","p","118",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"In meetings conducted via electronic media, the seconders shall signify their endorsement in accordance with the criteria and procedures prescribed by the Chairman."}]]]}]
a6:["$","p","119",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"A group of not less than 25 students may propose a motion concerning a grievance or any issue for the Council's consideration. The procedures and formats for such proposals shall conform to the notifications prescribed by the President of the Council."}]]]}]
a7:["$","p","120",{"id":"clause-40","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 40"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" For any motion placed on the meeting agenda, should the proposer intend to withdraw the motion, make amendments, withdraw their name as a co-proposer, or should a seconder intend to withdraw their endorsement, the prior consent of the assembly must be obtained."}]]]}]
a8:["$","p","121",{"id":"clause-41","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 41"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Once a motion has reached its respective agenda for consideration within the assembly, the proposal of an alternative motion sharing the same fundamental principle is prohibited. If the proposer or the amender fails to provide clarification before the assembly, or"}]]]}]
a9:["$","p","122",{"className":"m-0 border-t border-line pt-[var(--space-2)] text-sm text-ink-600","children":"[Page 13 of the original]"}]
aa:["$","p","123",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"is absent without an authorized representative to clarify on their behalf, said motion or amendment shall be deemed to have lapsed."}]]]}]
ab:["$","p","124",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"The authorization of a representative to provide clarification must be executed in writing and submitted to the President of the Council."}]]]}]
ac:["$","p","125",{"id":"clause-42","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 42"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Should a motion lapse, the resubmission of a motion sharing the same fundamental principle during the same meeting session is prohibited, unless it pertains to motions that have not yet been put to a vote, or motions expressly permitted by the President of the Council upon determination that the surrounding circumstances have materially changed."}]]]}]
ad:["$","p","126",{"id":"clause-43","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 43"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Any motion placed on the meeting agenda that remains unconsidered by the Council during that meeting session shall be deemed to have lapsed."}]]]}]
ae:["$","h5","127",{"className":"m-0 mt-[var(--space-4)]","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Part 3: Debate"}]]]}]
af:["$","p","128",{"id":"clause-44","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 44"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" The party vested with the first right of debate is the proposer of the motion or the amender. Should there be multiple proposers or amenders, the Chairman shall grant permission to only one individual to initiate the debate."}]]]}]
b0:["$","p","129",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"A commissioner who has reserved their opinion, a commissioner authorized by a commissioner who has reserved their opinion, or a commissioner authorized by an amender who has reserved their amendment at the committee level, shall hold a status equivalent to an amender."}]]]}]
b1:["$","p","130",{"id":"clause-45","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 45"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" In the presence of multiple debaters, the Chairman maintains the discretion to permit any individual to debate, provided that due consideration is afforded to the proposer, the amender, and those who have not yet participated in the debate."}]]]}]
b2:["$","p","131",{"className":"m-0 border-t border-line pt-[var(--space-2)] text-sm text-ink-600","children":"[Page 14 of the original]"}]
b3:["$","p","132",{"id":"clause-46","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 46"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" The debate must strictly adhere to or be directly relevant to the issue currently under consultation. It must not be superfluous, circular, repetitive, or duplicative. The unnecessary reading of documents to the assembly is prohibited, as is the introduction of any objects into the assembly for display, unless explicitly permitted by the Chairman."}]]]}]
b4:["$","p","133",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Debaters are strictly prohibited from exhibiting improper conduct or utilizing derogatory language, and shall not unnecessarily reference members or any individuals."}]]]}]
b5:["$","p","134",{"id":"clause-47","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 47"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Should the Chairman determine that an individual has debated sufficiently, the Chairman may direct said person to cease debating."}]]]}]
b6:["$","p","135",{"id":"clause-48","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 48"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Any member intending to protest an alleged violation of these rules or regulations must signify such intent by raising their hand above their head. The Chairman must afford the protesting member an opportunity to elucidate, whereupon the Chairman shall issue a ruling as to whether a violation has occurred."}]]]}]
b7:["$","p","136",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"In meetings conducted via electronic media, a member shall signify their intent to protest an alleged violation in accordance with the criteria and procedures prescribed by the Chairman."}]]]}]
b8:["$","p","137",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"The provisions set forth in paragraphs one and two shall apply mutatis mutandis to any individual who is the subject of a debate that improperly references personal matters or any other issues detrimental to said individual, including instances where they are referenced by name pursuant to Clause 19, paragraph two."}]]]}]
b9:["$","p","138",{"id":"clause-49","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 49"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Upon a protest being raised pursuant to Clause 48, the debater may voluntarily retract their statements or comply with the Chairman's ruling. If the debater departs the Council assembly without retracting their statements in accordance with the Chairman's"}]]]}]
ba:["$","p","139",{"className":"m-0 border-t border-line pt-[var(--space-2)] text-sm text-ink-600","children":"[Page 15 of the original]"}]
bb:["$","p","140",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"ruling, the Secretary-General shall document the non-compliance with the ruling in the meeting minutes."}]]]}]
bc:["$","p","141",{"id":"clause-50","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 50"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" The debate shall be deemed terminated when"}]]]}]
bd:["$","p","142",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(1) No individual desires to debate."}]]]}]
be:["$","p","143",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(2) The assembly resolves to close the debate."}]]]}]
bf:["$","p","144",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(3) The assembly resolves to raise another matter for consultation."}]]]}]
c0:["$","p","145",{"id":"clause-51","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 51"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" In circumstances where the Chairman deems the debate to have been sufficiently exhausted, the Chairman may request the assembly to issue a ruling on whether to formally close the debate."}]]]}]
c1:["$","p","146",{"id":"clause-52","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 52"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Upon the termination of the debate, further debate by any individual is prohibited, except in instances where the assembly is required to vote on the matter. In such cases, one of the individuals holding the initial right to debate on each motion shall be granted the right to deliver a final summary debate immediately prior to the assembly's vote."}]]]}]
c2:["$","p","147",{"id":"clause-53","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 53"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" If the Chairman issues a signal by striking a gavel, standing up, or employing any other appropriate method, the individual currently addressing the assembly must immediately cease speaking and be seated."}]]]}]
c3:["$","h5","148",{"className":"m-0 mt-[var(--space-4)]","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Part 4: Voting"}]]]}]
c4:["$","p","149",{"id":"clause-54","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 54"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" In circumstances necessitating a resolution of the Council, the Chairman shall issue a signal to notify the members prior to the commencement of voting."}]]]}]
c5:["$","p","150",{"className":"m-0 border-t border-line pt-[var(--space-2)] text-sm text-ink-600","children":"[Page 16 of the original]"}]
c6:["$","p","151",{"id":"clause-55","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 55"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Regarding the determination of a majority vote, should the assembly's opinions be divided into two or more factions, the faction securing the highest number of votes shall prevail."}]]]}]
c7:["$","p","152",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"In the event of a tie, the Chairman may either mandate a revote or prescribe an alternative voting methodology. Any utilization of an alternative voting methodology must be seconded by not less than two-thirds of the quorum."}]]]}]
c8:["$","p","153",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"The provisions of paragraph two shall apply primarily. Should a subsequent revote result in another tie, the Chairman shall cast the deciding vote."}]]]}]
c9:["$","p","154",{"id":"clause-56","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 56"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Voting shall be conducted openly. However, if a member proposes a motion, seconded by not less than two-thirds of the quorum, requesting a secret ballot, the voting shall proceed secretly."}]]]}]
ca:["$","p","155",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"In the event a member proposes a motion for a secret ballot pursuant to paragraph one, should another member raise an objection, seconded by not less than one-third of the quorum, the right to an open vote shall be maintained as a privilege."}]]]}]
cb:["$","p","156",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Voting by proxy is strictly prohibited."}]]]}]
cc:["$","p","157",{"id":"clause-57","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 57"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Open voting shall be executed via the following procedures:"}]]]}]
cd:["$","p","158",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(1) Raising a hand above the head."}]]]}]
ce:["$","p","159",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(2) Casting a vote with identified attribution via electronic media, as prescribed by the Chairman."}]]]}]
cf:["$","p","160",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(3) Any alternative method deemed appropriate by the assembly on a case-by-case basis."}]]]}]
d0:["$","p","161",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Regarding voting under (2), should the electronic media experience technical failure, the methodology shall be altered as prescribed by the Chairman."}]]]}]
d1:["$","p","162",{"className":"m-0 border-t border-line pt-[var(--space-2)] text-sm text-ink-600","children":"[Page 17 of the original]"}]
d2:["$","p","163",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Voting must primarily utilize the method under (1). Methods under (2) or (3) may only be employed upon a member's proposed motion approved by the assembly, during a meeting conducted via electronic media, or in the event of a vote recount pursuant to Clause 59."}]]]}]
d3:["$","p","164",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Regarding voting under paragraph two, if deemed appropriate by the Chairman, the Chairman shall appoint not less than three members to serve as vote counters."}]]]}]
d4:["$","p","165",{"id":"clause-58","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 58"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Secret voting shall be executed via the following procedures:"}]]]}]
d5:["$","p","166",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(1) Inscribing a mark upon a slip of paper, which is subsequently folded entirely closed. Those voting in favor shall write \"Approve\", those voting against shall write \"Disapprove\", and those abstaining shall write \"Abstain\"."}]]]}]
d6:["$","p","167",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(2) Casting an anonymous vote via electronic media, as prescribed by the Chairman."}]]]}]
d7:["$","p","168",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"(3) Any alternative method deemed appropriate by the assembly on a case-by-case basis."}]]]}]
d8:["$","p","169",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"The provisions set forth in Clause 57, paragraphs two, three, and four shall apply mutatis mutandis."}]]]}]
d9:["$","p","170",{"id":"clause-59","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 59"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Following a vote conducted pursuant to Clause 57 (1), if a member requests a recount, seconded by not less than ten members, a recount shall be executed by repeating the original procedure once."}]]]}]
da:["$","p","171",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"If a member requests a second recount, seconded by not less than ten members, the voting methodology shall transition to the methods under Clause 57 (2) or (3). However, a recount may not be requested if the margin of victory exceeds five votes."}]]]}]
db:["$","p","172",{"className":"m-0 border-t border-line pt-[var(--space-2)] text-sm text-ink-600","children":"[Page 18 of the original]"}]
dc:["$","p","173",{"id":"clause-60","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 60"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" For any motion lacking opposition, the Chairman shall inquire of the assembly whether any member holds a dissenting view. In the absence of dissent, the assembly shall be deemed to have passed a resolution approving said motion."}]]]}]
dd:["$","p","174",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"The Secretary-General shall compile a formal record of the individual voting of the Council members and shall disclose such record within the meeting minutes, via electronic media, or through other forms of information technology media, to ensure public awareness among students and the Thammasat community, with the exception of secret voting under Clause 58."}]]]}]
de:["$","h4","175",{"className":"m-0 mt-[var(--space-4)]","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Chapter 3 Committees"}]]]}]
df:["$","p","176",{"id":"clause-61","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 61"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" Ordinary committees may be established upon the approval of more than one-half of the total number of existing members of the Council."}]]]}]
e0:["$","p","177",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"A member must be affiliated with at least one ordinary committee, wherein the Office of the President of the Council and the Office of the Secretariat hold a status equivalent to an ordinary committee."}]]]}]
e1:["$","p","178",{"id":"clause-62","className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","strong","0",{"children":[["$","$3","0",{"children":"Clause 62"}]]}],["$","$3","1",{"children":" The establishment of an extraordinary committee may be executed to undertake a specific matter falling outside the scope of authority and duties of the ordinary committees, or as the Council otherwise deems appropriate."}]]]}]
e2:["$","p","179",{"className":"m-0 max-w-[var(--measure-th)] whitespace-pre-line","children":[[],[["$","$3","0",{"children":"An extraordinary committee shall be dissolved upon the completion of its designated undertaking."}]]]}]
e3:["$","p","180",{"className":"m-0 border-t border-line pt-[var(--space-2)] text-sm text-ink-600","children":"[Page 19 of the original]"}]
